 2. 🧑‍💻 Job worries persist 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios Americans are getting more worried about rising unemployment, but they're also more confident that they could find another job if they needed to, Axios' Neil Irwin and Courtenay Brown write from a new report . 

 📈 By the numbers: The perceived probability that unemployment will rise over the next year climbed to 45.3% in October, according to the New York Fed's Survey of Consumer Expectations.

 That's the highest since April 2020. Yes, but: People's perceived probability of finding another job if they lost their current position rose to 46.5%, the highest in about a year.

 🤔 The mixed sentiment underscores the weirdness in today's labor market: Hiring is picking up and unemployment remains low, but it can be tough to find work.

