 4. 👩‍🚀 1 for the road: Astronauts wanted 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios NASA is now accepting applications for new astronauts for its Artemis lunar program.

 Aspiring candidates have until Dec. 3 to submit their applications. Final selections are expected by late 2027. 🚀 With only 32 active astronauts, the space agency needs more recruits as it looks to expand humanity's presence beyond low-Earth orbit.

 Artemis III commander Randy Bresnik tells AP: "We have far more work than we have astronauts." Go deeper ... How to apply . 

 
 
